<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H552</pnldref><english><title>Procure homosexual acts</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>PROCURATION</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>PROCURED</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>MAN</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>BUGGERY</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>PROCURING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>4</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>SEXUAL OFFENCES ACT 1967</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>MALE</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>MEN</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>BOY</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..), being a man, procured **(..SPECIFY NAME..), another man to commit with a third man an act of buggery   which by reason of section 1 of the Sexual Offences Act 1967 was not an offence</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to section 4(1) of the Sexual Offences Act 1967.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt; being a man&lt;br /&gt; procured another man&lt;br /&gt; to commit lawful homosexual acts&lt;br /&gt; with a third man</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA6</code><description>Offences brought to justice scheme</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>THIS OFFENCE IS NOW OBSOLETE&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;(i) The consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions is required where one of the parties is under 16 years of age.&lt;br /&gt;(ii) It is not an offence for a man to procure another man for an act of gross indecency if, by reason of section 1 of the Sexual Offences Act 1967, the two men are not committing an offence under section 13 of the Sexual Offences Act 1956.&lt;br /&gt;(iii) As amended by the Sexual Offences (Amendment) Act 2000.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><description>EITHER WAY</description></modeoftrial><timelimitforprosecutions>None</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>SUMMARY:  Six months imprisonment and / or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.&lt;br /&gt;INDICTMENT: Two years imprisonment.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;None</penalty><geographicregion><code>EW</code><description>England and Wales</description><